OL,3,GNEWSASurrey council backs decision
OL,4,Aagainst Ulez signs
OL,5,
OL,6,FA county council has stood by its
OL,7,Fdecision not to allow Ultra Low
OL,8,FEmission Zone (Ulez) signs and cameras,
OL,9,Fdespite more than #15m in fines being
OL,10,Fissued to residents.
OL,12,FIn 2023, Surrey County Council (SCC)
OL,13,Fopposed the expansion into the outer
OL,14,FLondon suburbs and refused to install
OL,15,Fsignage.
OL,17,FSCC's transport lead Matt Furniss said:
OL,18,F"This situation remains unchanged as
OL,19,Fsadly none of the mitigation measures
OL,20,Fput forward to support Surrey residents
OL,21,Fhave been put in place by the Mayor of
OL,22,FLondon or Transport for London (TfL)."
OL,23,APub: 09-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,327,320,200,140,0,100
